eliezer (0.6.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Set the package version to 0.6.0, as requested.
  * Add `eliezer transcribe PATH... --out DIR`: transcribes audio files (or directories, with `--recursive`) one after the other
    through `POST /v1/audio/transcriptions` and writes `txt`, `srt`, `vtt` and `json` outputs built from one `verbose_json`
    answer. Existing outputs are kept (resumable), outputs are written atomically, `--dry-run`, `--limit`, `--replace`,
    `--prompt-file` and `--timeout-secs` are supported; a failing file does not stop the run.
  * Prioritize diffusion models on the GPU: add `[cpu] ram_budget_gb` and a per-model
    `device = "auto" | "gpu" | "cpu"` (also a `device` field of the load request). While an image model
    loads, is loaded or is waiting, language models left to `auto` run on the CPU (llama.cpp with no GPU
    layers) instead of evicting it, and they fall back to the CPU when the GPU is too small. The planner
    works per memory pool, a 409 on the CPU names `[cpu] ram_budget_gb`, `/api/v1/status` and `eliezer ps`
    show the device and the CPU memory. Without a RAM budget nothing changes.
  * Add `DELETE /api/v1/models/pins/{org}/{repo}` and `eliezer rm ORG/REPO`: delete a repository fetched with
    `eliezer get`/`download`; refused while a download runs or a configured model uses its files. Only
    directories with a pin file are touched.
  * Add `POST /v1/images/edits` (multipart, one to four pictures, as in the OpenAI API) for image models with the new
    `extra.image_edit = true`, and `capabilities.image_edit` in the model list. The pictures are checked (type by first
    bytes, 20 MB each, at most four) and handed to `sd-server` as reference pictures. Checked live with FLUX.2 klein 4B:
    a fox edited blue in 27 s at 1024x1024. New dependency: axum feature `multipart` (crate `multer`).
  * Add music models (MiniMax Music 3): `kind = "music"` with `backend = "audiocpp"` (new `[backend.audiocpp]` with `program`,
    `port_range`, `compute`, `library_path`), served by `audiocpp_server` of audio.cpp as a child process per loaded model, and
    `POST /v1/audio/speech` (lyrics as `input`, the description as `instructions`, WAV as the answer) with
    `capabilities.music_generation`. The package directory is `source.file`; `extra` takes `language_model`, `rvq_depth_decoder`,
    `flow_transformer`, `duration_sec`, `steps` and `cfg_scale`. `scripts/build-audiocpp.sh` builds the program (pinned commit,
    HIP); `scripts/build-deb.sh rocm` bundles it as `/usr/libexec/<triplet>/eliezer/audiocpp_server`. Checked live on the Radeon RX
    7900 XTX: a 20 s song in 1 min 20 s (including the load), a 30 s song in 2 min 32 s.
  * Add speech recognition: `kind = "stt"` with `backend = "whispercpp"` (new `[backend.whispercpp]`), served by `whisper-server` of
    whisper.cpp as a child process per loaded model, and `POST /v1/audio/transcriptions` (OpenAI shape; `json`, `text`,
    `verbose_json`, `srt`, `vtt`) with `type: "stt"` and `capabilities.transcription`. The service decodes MP3, M4A/AAC, Ogg, FLAC and
    WAV itself, cuts long recordings into overlapping pieces and joins the segments; limits and piece length are settings.
    New dependencies: `symphonia` 0.5.5 and `rubato` 0.16.2 (pure Rust). The program itself was not run yet (docs/Runtimes.md).
  * A picture request that fails no longer takes the model down: a request the program refused is answered with 400,
    and a picture that could not be drawn marks the model as crashed only when its program no longer answers.
    Before, any failure marked the model failed, which dropped it and the jobs other requests had running on it.
  * Add `extra.tokenizer` (path of an external `tokenizer.json`, passed to `sd-server` as `--tokenizer`) for MOSS-Image, which
    needs the Qwen3.5 vocabulary. Checked live with MOSS-Image-SFT Q8_0.
  * A command without its required arguments prints its usage (the template of the help text) with exit code 2, for
    example `eliezer download`.
  * `eliezer status` and `eliezer ps` list downloads that run or wait, with percent and bytes.
  * Show the download progress of `eliezer get`/`download` in one line rewritten in place on a terminal; in a
    pipe the line still changes only in steps of 5 %.
  * Add `POST /api/v1/models/estimate`: the memory Eliezer calculates for a model, context and parallelism,
    with its parts (weights, KV cache, overhead), the fit in the GPU and CPU pools and the largest
    context that fits, so MultiGPT can show Eliezer's figures instead of its own size-based guess.
  * Suggest the `reasoning` options of a model from its chat template when importing: effort levels for
    gpt-oss, on/off for Qwen and Gemma 4 (with the template's own default), both for Qwen3.8 (`xhigh` default).
    Without the line the model list reports no `capabilities.reasoning` and MultiGPT cannot offer thinking levels.
  * Describe vision models in the configuration: `source.projector` (the mmproj file), `vision = true` and
    `projector_gb`; the memory estimate counts the projector, and `--import`/`--suggest` pair a model with the
    projector in its directory. Reading images in the llama.cpp runtime is the next step and is not part of this change.
  * Add the search of Hugging Face (M5-00): `GET /api/v1/hub/search` and `GET /api/v1/hub/models/{org}/{repo}`,
    `eliezer search` and `eliezer inspect`. They list candidates with license, quantizations, file sizes, backend
    support and the fit in the GPU and RAM budgets. Nothing is downloaded and no token is sent;
    `[huggingface] search = false` switches it off. New crate `eliezer-hub` with `reqwest` (rustls).
  * Read images with the llama.cpp runtime: a model with `source.projector` accepts `image_url` parts (base64 `data:`
    URIs only, never links) in the OpenAI and the Anthropic dialect. Checked on a Radeon RX 7900 XTX with olmOCR 2 7B,
    Qwen3.8 27B and Gemma 4 26B, which all read back the numbers on a drawn page. A model without projector refuses
    images with 400. The micro-batch steps down (2048, 1024, 512) until the context of a vision model can be created.
  * Keep only the window of sliding-window layers in the cache (`swa_full` off), as the memory estimate assumes:
    Gemma 4 at 32 768 tokens took 25.4 GB of VRAM instead of 19.7 GB. Prefix reuse and parallel requests still pass
    the live check on Gemma 4 and gpt-oss.
  * Translate the German leftovers in the Anthropic error messages.
  * Fetch models from Hugging Face (M5-01 to M5-03): `POST /api/v1/models/download`, `eliezer get ORG/REPO` (picks the
    best quantization that fits, with the vision projector) and `eliezer download ORG/REPO FILE...`. Only repositories
    on `[huggingface] allow` are fetched; files go to `<models_dir>/<Organisation>/<Repository>/`, are resumed after an
    interruption, checked against the listed SHA-256 and size and renamed only when they match. Each repository
    directory records a pin (commit, sizes, hashes); `eliezer pins [--verify]` and `GET /api/v1/models/pins` report
    deviations, and the service logs them at start. `cache_limit_gb` is enforced (507), gated repositories answer
    403 with a license notice. The token comes from `huggingface.token_file` (0600, otherwise not used) or `HF_TOKEN`
    and never appears in arguments, logs or messages; `scripts/check-secrets.sh` checks that. New dependency `sha2`.
  * Accept a system prompt for models whose chat template rejects the system role (Mistral 7B v0.3 answered 400 "does
    not fit the context window" to a system plus user message): the text goes in front of the first user message,
    checked live on Mistral in both dialects. Name a missing configuration section or field in the error message.
    A file download is no longer cut off by the 15 s limit of metadata requests (found with the first real download).
  * Serve image models with stable-diffusion.cpp (M6): each loaded model is an `sd-server` child process on a loopback
    port (`[backend.sdcpp]`), started without a shell, with a cleared environment and arguments from the configuration;
    `/v1/images/generations` returns PNG images. New model settings `extra.steps`, `extra.cfg_scale`,
    `extra.sampling_method` and `extra.offload_to_cpu`. A router sends models to llama.cpp or stable-diffusion.cpp. Checked
    live with Qwen Image 2.1 (a photographic fox in 13 s at 512x512, 80 s at 1024x1024) and the GPU priority: Mistral
    ran on the CPU while the image model held the GPU. `[backend.sdcpp] library_path` names the directories with the
    libraries the program needs (it has no run path). The ROCm package contains `sd-server` (built by `scripts/build-sdcpp.sh`) in
    the multiarch libexec directory `/usr/libexec/<triplet>/eliezer/` (run path `$ORIGIN/../../../lib/<triplet>/eliezer`
    to the libraries in the private directory, also `libomp`), so `[backend.sdcpp] program` is
    `/usr/libexec/x86_64-linux-gnu/eliezer/sd-server` and no library path is needed.
  * The estimate of a model with a fixed figure (`vram_gb` or a measurement, as for image models) puts the figure in
    `weights_bytes`, so the parts add up to the total (MultiGPT showed 0.0 GB for Qwen Image from the empty parts).
  * Add a prompt helper for image models: `extra.prompt_helper` names a language model that writes a detailed English description
    from a short wish before the picture is drawn (on the CPU when a RAM budget exists, so the image model keeps the GPU).
    `enhance_prompt` in the request switches it, the answer has `prompt_enhanced` and `revised_prompt`; a helper that fails
    leaves the original prompt in use. Checked live with Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct (fetched with `eliezer get`, Q4_K_M, also reads
    images through its projector; about 10 tokens/s on the CPU, a description in 6 s) and Qwen Image 2.1.
  * Take wildcards in the download allowlist: `*` stands for any run of characters in the organisation or in the repository name
    (`*/Qwen3-VL*`, `mradermacher/*GGUF`); `*/*` is refused. `**/Qwen*` works as a pattern now instead of stopping a reload.
  * Never pass a refusal of the prompt helper on as the prompt: a stock model sometimes answers a wish with "I cannot ..." (in the
    language of the wish). Refusals, questions, German or overlong answers count as `declined`, the original prompt is drawn and the
    answer says `"prompt_helper": "declined"` (`used`, `off`, `failed` otherwise).
  * Draw a new picture for every image request: `sd-server` started with its default seed 42 and returned the same picture for
    the same prompt every time (found when two identical requests gave identical files). It starts with `--seed -1` now, and
    `/v1/images/generations` takes an optional `seed` for repeatable results. Checked live: without a seed two requests differ,
    with seed 7 twice they are identical.
  * Report `capabilities.image_generation: true` for image models and `capabilities.ocr: true` for models marked `ocr = true`
    in the configuration (a text recognition model needs `vision`; `--import` and `--suggest` set it for vision models whose
    name says OCR) in the model list, so MultiGPT can map the capability instead of guessing; `eliezer ls` shows `image`
    and `ocr`.
  * Show a size for models without `size_gb` (the size of their files; an image model counts its text encoder and VAE too) and no
    context window for image models in the model list and `eliezer ls`.
  * Accept the histories chat programs send to models with a strict chat template (Mistral): the same role twice in a row, an
    assistant turn first, a system message in the middle, tool calls and results. They are reshaped (joined turns, tool turns as
    plain text, the system text in front of the first user turn) when the template refuses them; before, they answered 400. Checked
    live on Mistral with seven shapes that failed.
  * Keep the command line client tests independent of the user's own ~/.config/eliezer/api_key.
  * Update the installation example to eliezer_0.6.0-1_amd64.deb.

 -- Jörg Bernau <Joerg.Bernau@web.de>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:17:18 +0200

